exclusions:
  template-job-rule:
    reason: >-
      Envoy metrics in the dis-edge Azure Managed Prometheus workspaces are
      identified by OpenTelemetry resource labels (k8s_cluster_name,
      k8s_namespace_name, envoy_cluster_name, ...), not by a meaningful
      job/instance pair, so a job template would only add a dropdown that
      filters nothing useful.
    entries:
      - dashboard: Envoy Clusters
      - dashboard: Envoy Global
      - dashboard: Global Ratelimit
      - dashboard: Resources Monitor
      - dashboard: SLA Envoy Gateway / Edge
  template-instance-rule:
    reason: >-
      No instance template by design; see template-job-rule.
    entries:
      - dashboard: Envoy Clusters
      - dashboard: Envoy Global
      - dashboard: Global Ratelimit
      - dashboard: Resources Monitor
      - dashboard: SLA Envoy Gateway / Edge
  target-job-rule:
    reason: >-
      Queries filter on the OpenTelemetry resource labels and the dashboard
      variables instead of job; see template-job-rule.
    entries:
      - dashboard: Envoy Clusters
      - dashboard: Envoy Global
      - dashboard: Global Ratelimit
      - dashboard: Resources Monitor
      - dashboard: SLA Envoy Gateway / Edge
  target-instance-rule:
    reason: >-
      Queries filter on the OpenTelemetry resource labels and the dashboard
      variables instead of instance; see template-job-rule.
    entries:
      - dashboard: Envoy Clusters
      - dashboard: Envoy Global
      - dashboard: Global Ratelimit
      - dashboard: Resources Monitor
      - dashboard: SLA Envoy Gateway / Edge
  panel-title-description-rule:
    reason: >-
      Imported from the upstream Envoy Gateway dashboards, whose panels have
      self-explanatory titles but no descriptions. Not worth diverging from
      upstream for.
    entries:
      - dashboard: Envoy Clusters
      - dashboard: Envoy Global
      - dashboard: Resources Monitor
  panel-datasource-rule:
    reason: >-
      These panels use the "-- Mixed --" datasource; every target inside them
      still uses the templated $datasource.
    entries:
      - dashboard: Resources Monitor
  target-rate-interval-rule:
    reason: >-
      The SLA tiles use fixed windows (5m, 15m, 1h, ...) on purpose, so each
      tile shows exactly what the matching alert would evaluate regardless of
      the time picker. $__rate_interval would make them drift from the alerts.
    entries:
      - dashboard: SLA Envoy Gateway / Edge
